Cyde Weys wrote:
>
> What is a pudding farm?

When you hit a black pudding with an iron weapon that does at
least one point of damage there is a good chance it will
divide into two black puddings of the same size (but half
the hit points IIRC).

One goal is to know what weapons are iron and what weapons
aren't.  Some are far from obvious.  Another goal is to get
your weapon to cause only one point of damage as causing
more cuts the maximum possible number of splits, like when
fighting a gremlin over water.

I wonder if the black puddings gain hit points and heal.
If they do then it doesn't converge the way fighting
gremlins over water does.

Another goal is to survive the process.  Black puddings are
nontrivial opponents for inexperienced characters.

> And how does it raise your AC?

One of the benefits of prayer.  Lots of corpses, lots of
chances to reconcile.  Cause one hit point on a monster that
only has one hit point, pick it up, move one square to the
altar, #offer.  Lather rinse repeat.

When eaten black puddings confer several intrinsics so AC
is not the only potential benefit.  Since pudding farming
is done at an altar there's the choice to just #offer and
not pray so artifacts are also a potential crop to be
harvested.  Since there are death-drop items farming is
also a way to gather random items.

Since black puddings are formidible monsters for an
inexperienced character, farming is also a good way to die.
A caution I felt worth repeating.

